  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Honeywell International has received $257M in federal contract obligations so far in FY2026 to date. Honeywell International won 208 awards this fiscal year to date, with an average award size of $1.2M, and obligations fell 58.9% year over year. Department of Defense accounted for $257M of obligations in FY2026 to date. Military Armored Vehicle, Tank, and Tank Component Manufacturing is the largest market for Honeywell International in FY2026 to date at $153M, followed by Aircraft Manufacturing at $81.6M and Aircraft Engine and Engine Parts Manufacturing at $14.1M. Historical obligations show variability, with FY24 at $696M, FY25 at $626M, FY23 at $489M, FY22 at $536M, and FY21 at $437M. National Aeronautics and Space Administration reported $0 in obligations for FY2026 to date. Some reported markets show $0 obligations for FY2026 to date, including Fluid Power Valve and Hose Fitting Manufacturing and Industrial Valve Manufacturing.",
