        "body": "FY2026 to date obligations for Honeywell International are $257M compared with FY25 at $626M and FY24 at $696M. Obligations were $489M in FY23, $536M in FY22, and $437M in FY21. The reported year-over-year change for FY2026 to date is down 58.9%."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies and markets dominate Honeywell International's federal business?",
        "body": "Department of Defense is the primary buyer, accounting for $257M in FY2026 to date. Military Armored Vehicle, Tank, and Tank Component Manufacturing is the largest market at $153M, followed by Aircraft Manufacturing at $81.6M and Aircraft Engine and Engine Parts Manufacturing at $14.1M."
      }
